docs/backlog.md:109:**D161 — DEVDESK-510 (NX-07): a refused members endpoint is a typed error, not an empty group. Decided (plan `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-510-plan.md`, implemented on branch `feat/devdesk-510-nexus-members-refused`, archived 2026-11-18; the wording validated by the user, and the transient `unreachable` state decided by the user on 2026-11-18): (1) `registrymgr.MembersRefusedError` (`Group`, `Status`, `Anonymous`, `Cause` → `*oci.StatusError`, `Is` `ErrMembersRefused`, `Unwrap` to the status error) is returned for a 401 or 403 from the management API on `GET /v1/repositories/{format}/group/{name}` only; the anonymous retry decides when the first attempt was refused. Network failure, deadline, 404, 5xx, off-origin redirect and unreadable reply are propagated and not cached (D23); an empty member list is a settled empty group, not an error. Its text carries the group and the status, never a URL, header or body. Rejected: a bare sentinel (it cannot say whether the request was anonymous), a result struct (interface churn). (2) The group cache file `registry-groups.json` moves to the envelope `{"version":2,"groups","refusals"}`. A refusal sits beside the listing, never inside it, and never touches the members known (D23); a successful listing, even empty, clears it. A legacy bare-map file keeps only the entries with a member, the empty ones are set aside (CA6), so they read as `never`; a version 2 or newer file is read as it is (a downgrade is accepted). One decoder, shared with the read-only MCP reader; writes are atomic, `0600`. (3) UI: the Members cell reads `denied` (`denied · N known · age` when a list survives), the status line is derived on every render (Warn for a refusal, Info for a settled empty group), and a transient failure reads `unreachable` in the footer at level Error with nothing cached. The Members column stays `SizingContent` with `MinWidth` 16, so the visibility threshold does not move. Members declared by hand are listed at group level. (4) MCP `registries_list` gains `members_refused` (`at`, `age_seconds`, `status`, `anonymous`), never an error text. (5) The follow-ups of D160 are done here: the `format` segment is escaped with `url.PathEscape`, and the logs use `%q` for the server's `type` and `format`. Out of scope, recorded: `refusedStatus` in `internal/imagesearch/verdict.go` (a management-API status is not yet told apart from a registry refusal; no Nexus path reaches it today); `repoName` is not escaped in the endpoints; the names of members returned by the server are not validated, and ANSI sequences in the table cells are pre-existing; concurrent writes of the group cache are last-writer-wins (pre-existing lost-update race, a candidate follow-up with one cache instance or a file lock); the hypothesis that the detail endpoint answers 403 to a pull-only account is to confirm on the NX-03 bench; nit: the status line reads `1 declared by hand are used`. No ADR: local, derived data, reversible by a revert (a revert reads the v2 file as empty groups, `never`). **Plane:** DEVDESK-510 (NX-07); NX-09 (DEVDESK, depends on NX-07) can now read `unknown` from the refusal. Sources: `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-510-plan.md`, `internal/registrymgr/refusal.go`, `internal/registrymgr/nexus.go`, `internal/cache/registry_groups.go`, `internal/ui/oci_resources/members_refused.go`, `internal/mcp/registry_tools.go`; D23, D160.**
docs/backlog.md:111:**D160 — DEVDESK-509 (NX-06): the Nexus REST client handles errors like the `internal/oci` registry client. Decided (plan `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-509-plan.md`, 2026-11-17): (1) The client reuses `internal/oci`: a third source, `oci.SourceManagementAPI`, in `oci.StatusError` (`management API returned <code>`), for a registry manager's own REST API. No copy, no new package, no import cycle (`internal/oci` depends on no other `devdesk` package). Rejected: a `registrymgr.StatusError` (a second type for one concept) and an extracted `internal/httpguard` (out of proportion here). (2) A non-200 answer is a `*oci.StatusError` with no status line, body or header echoed, so no secret reaches the error. A context error is never a `StatusError`: a failed body read returns `read Nexus response: <ctx error>` (wrapped with `%w`) when the context is done, so `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled | context.DeadlineExceeded)` holds whatever `net/http` returns. (3) The 1 MiB reply cap (`maxNexusResponse`) stays in `nexus.go`, not shared with the token cap (`maxTokenResponse`), which bounds another reply. (4) Behaviour change: a 200 reply that is empty, or valid JSON with no `type` (`{}`, `null`), is a failed discovery (`errEmptyReply`, `errNoRepositoryType`, wrapped with the endpoint), not cached as "not a group" (D23); the members last known are kept. Hypothesis, to confirm in review: Nexus always sends `type` on `GET /service/rest/v1/repositories/{name}`. Syntax errors were already rejected. (5) Criteria 1 and 2 (same-origin redirect and 1 MiB cap) shipped with DEVDESK-412 (D156); this entry adds only tests: another scheme, and 302 and 307 for the off-origin refusal. No ADR: local and reversible by a revert. Follow-ups, out of scope: NX-07 (`fetchRepoMeta` and `fetchGroupMembers` swallow the step-2 errors, so a failure erases the members known); `internal/imagesearch/verdict.go` (`refusedStatus`) should test `Source == oci.SourceRegistry` rather than `!= SourceToken`, so a management-API `StatusError` is not read as a refusal (no Nexus path reaches it today); `internal/registrymgr/nexus.go` logs `result.Type` and `result.Format` with `%s`, so a hostile server can inject ANSI sequences or newlines into the logs: use `%q`. **Plane:** DEVDESK-509 (NX-06). Sources: `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-509-plan.md`, `internal/oci/registry.go`, `internal/registrymgr/nexus.go`, `internal/registrymgr/nexus_errors_test.go`; D142, D156.**
